{"id": "EUVD-2026-106914", "enisaUuid": "7e225775-3491-39d3-a3ee-0d36dd4b28f7", "description": "sharp before 0.35.5 bundles a librsvg dependency affected by a memory-related vulnerability (CVE-2026-96889) that, under certain runtime-specific conditions, can lead to code execution on glibc-based Linux. An attacker can supply a crafted SVG image that, when decoded by sharp through librsvg, may result in arbitrary code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:37:10", "baseScore": 8.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/lovell/sharp/security/advisories/GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sharp-before-0.35.5-rce-via-librsvg-dependency-memory-vulnerability"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j56w-ppx9-7qff", "CVE-2026-114111"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4b5d5f9a-69d4-33ce-b2c1-c20300f099d2", "product": {"name": "sharp", "vendor": {"name": "code16"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.35.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f66d67fe-9064-327d-9e2a-839efb9aa418", "vendor": {"name": "lovell"}}], "isExploited": false}